From: xinyang <xinyangmn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: quiesce capture before stopping the ISP

The isolated IPA's synchronous stop dispatches events while waiting for its
reply. SoftwareIsp has already stopped its worker at that point, but the
video buffer-ready signal is still connected. A captured frame can therefore
queue a Debayer invocation on the stopped worker. Teardown then cancels the
request and releases its buffers, leaving the invocation to replay invalid
pointers when the worker starts again.

Disconnect capture delivery before stopping the ISP. Keep the existing
blocking worker stop, worker wait and owner callback drain; release buffers
only after those have completed. SimpleCameraData is not an Object, so the
video signal calls it directly and has no separate queued delivery to drain.

--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1710,6 +1710,13 @@
 							 &DelayedControls::applyControls);
 	}

+	/*
+	 * A synchronous IPA stop may dispatch capture events while the software
+	 * ISP worker is already stopped. Quiesce the producer before that call
+	 * so no buffer pointers can be queued for the worker's next start.
+	 */
+	video->bufferReady.disconnect(data, &SimpleCameraData::imageBufferReady);
+
 	if (data->useConversion_) {
 		if (data->converter_)
 			data->converter_->stop();
@@ -1720,8 +1727,6 @@
 	video->streamOff();
 	video->releaseBuffers();

-	video->bufferReady.disconnect(data, &SimpleCameraData::imageBufferReady);
-
 	data->clearIncompleteRequests();
 	data->conversionBuffers_.clear();

